※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4933 LANG_MARK_NOT_NEEDED

※ `@[io]` says a function does input or output without being handed a device
※ to do it with.  One that does none -- here it adds two numbers -- says what is
※ not so, and is refused as a needless `@[impure]` is.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[io]
fn sum(a: u8, b: u8) → u8:
    a + b

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if sum(1u8, 2u8) = 3u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
